y Mike's Subs Inc. engages in franchising and operating fast casual, submarine-style sandwich restaurants specializing in authentic, hand-crafted, and craveable subs. The company also offers catering services, as well as provides mobile app, online ordering, and third-party delivery. It operates stores in the United States and Canada, as well as franchise agreements in the United Kingdom and Ireland. The company was founded in 1956 and is based in Tinton Falls, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles R. Morrison | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 899 people. Revenue per employee of $805K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Jersey Mike's Subs Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $6.0B market cap on $724M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $221M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 162% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.6170615259886496},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (82% sell ratio, net $1418.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Jersey Mike\u2019s (NYSE:JMKE) Announces Special Dividend of $0.35","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/jersey-mikes-nysejmke-announces-special-dividend-of-0-35.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793707862.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Jersey Mike\u2019s (NYSE:JMKE) Stock Gets Price Target Trim from Sanford C. Bernstein","source":"thelincol